ce the parameters that go here are not all obvious.\n;\n; Format:\n;   [section] ; section goes between []\n;   param=value ; assign values to parameters\n\nconfig_version=5\n\n[application]\n\nconfig/name=\"Minimap marker logic and zoom control\"\nconfig/description=\"A simple task to test CUA ability to move a player asset to the origin coordinates\"\nrun/main_scene=\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"\nconfig/features=PackedStringArray(\"4.4\")\n\n[rendering]\n\nrenderer/rendering_method=\"gl_compatibility\"\n```\n- **Godot version**: 4.4\n- **Renderer**: GL Compatibility (gl_compatibility)\n- **Main scene**: `res://scenes/main.tscn`\n- **Project name**: \"Minimap marker logic and zoom control\"\n\n---\n\n## 5. `task_config.json`\n\n```json\n{\n  \"instruction\": \"Implement the minimap logic: export a Player reference and a zoom property with a clamped setter, cache the grid and marker prototypes, center the player marker after the first frame, compute grid_scale from the grid size and viewport, duplicate and show markers for every node in the minimap_objects group using their minimap_icon keys, store them in a 'markers' dictionary, rotate (player rotation + PI/2) and position markers each frame relative to the player (scaling to 0.75 and clamping when off the grid), implement _on_object_removed which removes and erases markers when called, and implement _on_gui_input which handles mouse wheel gui_input to adjust zoom. Ensure the world scene connects minimap_objects \\\"removed\\\" signals to the minimap while mobs/crates have the \\\"removed\\\" signals, expose each one's \\\"minimap_icon\\\", and ensure mobs/crates belong to the minimap_objects group.\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Additional Configuration Files\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg`\nRegisters three global class names: `Crate` (extends Area2D), `Mob` (extends CharacterBody2D), and `Player` (extends CharacterBody2D). `minimap.gd` and `world.gd` are NOT registered as class_name scripts.\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/scene_groups_cache.cfg`\nEmpty -- no scene groups are currently defined.\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/editor/project_metadata.cfg`\n```\n[editor_metadata]\nexecutable_path=\"/run/gamedevbench-bin/godot\"\n\n[recent_files]\nscenes=[\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"]\n```\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/editor/main.tscn-folding-3ad5c15c4f3250da0cc7c1af1770d85f.cfg`\nTracks editor folding state for the main scene's node tree (all nodes currently unfolded).\n\n### `/workspace/.godot/editor/filesystem_cache10`\nFull filesystem cache listing all project files with type information and dependency chains.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThis is a **Godot 4.4** project designed as a coding exercise for implementing minimap functionality. It contains:\n\n- **5 GDScript files** (all essentially stubs with TODOs except `player.gd` which has basic movement logic)\n- **5 Scene files** (`main.tscn` is the entry point; it instances the minimap, player, a mob at (120,0), and a crate at (-160,0))\n- **5 PNG assets** for the minimap (wood frame, blueprint paper grid, arrow icon, red jewel icon, yellow exclamation icon) with their `.import` and `.res` files\n- The `task_config.json` provides detailed instructions on what needs to be implemented across `minimap.gd`, `world.gd`, `mob.gd`, and `crate.gd`\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f22f32043ffeu3Xi7cl3mt0ntr","sessionId":"ses_f22f2e9b3fferKy3TPGd3qOhu5","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore project structure","time":{"start":1790415017552,"end":1790415165016}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_cc0a3795-04a5-44da-876e-64fa795ed041"}},"id":"prt_0dd0d1642001jXm0EC4ZnnfpfB","sessionID":"ses_f22f32043ffeu3Xi7cl3mt0ntr","messageID":"msg_0dd0ce172001tDZJoJ2XXLZhO0"}}
